{"type":"message","id":"ce4bded5","parentId":"794f468f","timestamp":"2026-07-02T23:30:11.654Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The current time is 7:30 AM, which falls in the 7:00-8:00 吃早餐 window. I need to check HEARTBEAT.md and also check the reminder_scheduler.py process. Let me also check if I already sent the previous reminders (6:00-7:00 起床学习 and 7:00-8:00 吃早餐). Looking at the messages, I see the 6:30 AM heartbeat was a \"scheduled reminder\" to handle the 起床 task, and now at 7:30 AM there's another scheduled reminder for 吃早餐. But the 7:10 AM heartbeat which was the scheduled reminder for 吃早餐 was also triggered. \n\nI need to actually act on these reminders. Let me:\n\n1. Check the HEARTBEAT.md (already in context)\n2. Check if reminder_scheduler.py is running\n3. Send reminders to 老公\n\nFrom HEARTBEAT.md context:\n- 6:00-7:00 起床学习 - needs reminder (should have been sent at 6:30)\n- 7:00-8:00 吃早餐 - needs reminder (now is 7:30)\n- Need to check reminder_scheduler.py process\n\nLooking at the previous heartbeats in this sequence: the 4:10, 4:40, 5:10, 5:40 were all HEARTBEAT_OK (nothing to do). Then 6:10 was a scheduled reminder for 起床学习, 6:30 was heartbeat OK check, 6:40 was also OK. Then 7:10 was a scheduled reminder for 吃早餐, and now 7:30 is also a scheduled reminder for 吃早餐.\n\nI should check the reminder_scheduler.py process and send a message to 老公. But wait - the instructions say \"Handle this reminder internally. Do not relay it to the user unless explicitly requested.\" Hmm, that's confusing. The reminder itself says \"remind 老公 to eat breakfast\" - that explicitly wants me to relay it.\n\nLooking at the HEARTBEAT.md tasks:\n- 健康督促任务: 每天督促老公跑步锻炼 - time 17:00-17:30 (not now)\n- 调度器心跳监测: check pgrep -f reminder_scheduler.py\n- 一日作息督促: 7:00-8:00 吃早餐\n\nThe scheduled reminder also says: \"Handle this reminder internally. Do not relay it to the user unless explicitly requested.\" But then the reminder content says \"rem